<h1>Projects</h1>

<p>Things built and being built — radio, Linux, microcontrollers. Each
project states its own code license on its page; the site footer's
CC&nbsp;BY-NC-SA notice covers prose, not code.</p>

{# Projects are grouped to match the about page's arc: assistive
   technology first, then data, then radio, then the everyday tools that
   don't belong to any of those. Every project's front matter needs a
   `group` (one of the names below), an `order` within it, and a
   `language` — the primary language or technology, shown after the
   summary. #}
{% set groups = ["Assistive technology", "Data", "Amateur radio", "Tools"] %}
{% set projects = collections.projects | sort(attribute="data.order") %}
{% if projects.length %}
{% for g in groups %}
{% set grouped = projects | inGroup(g) %}
{% if grouped.length %}
<h2>{{ g }}</h2>
<ul>
{% for p in grouped %}
  <li><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.data.title }}</a>{% if p.data.summary %} — {{ p.data.summary }}{% endif %}{% if p.data.language %} · {{ p.data.language }}{% endif %}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
<p><em>Nothing written up yet. The bench is not empty — the write-ups
just haven't caught up.</em></p>
{% endif %}
